1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,260
Sci-fi movies tend to capture children's imaginations and have long been part of students' excited chats in the schoolyard.
科幻电影往往能吸引孩子们的想象力，并长期以来成为学生们在校园里兴奋讨论的话题。

2
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:17,910
But now a scientific journal has urged at least one sci-fi movie to be shown in class by science teachers.
但现在，一份科学期刊呼吁科学教师至少在课堂上放映一部科幻电影。

3
00:00:17,910 --> 00:00:30,620
Scientific papers published in the American Journal of Physics (AJP) and in Classical and Quantum Gravity have seen merit in the way the movie Interstellar portrays wormholes.
发表在《美国物理学杂志》（AJP）和《经典与量子引力》上的科学论文认为，电影《星际穿越》对虫洞描绘的方式很有价值。

4
00:00:30,620 --> 00:00:36,630
Dr David Jackson from AJP said publishing this paper "was a no-brainer".
AJP的大卫·杰克逊博士表示，发表这篇论文“是理所当然的”。

5
00:00:36,630 --> 00:00:43,240
He added: "The physics has been very carefully reviewed by experts and found to be accurate.
他补充说：“电影中的物理内容已经经过专家的仔细审查，并被发现是准确的。

6
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:52,400
The publication will encourage physics teachers to show the film in their classes to get across ideas about general relativity".
这篇论文将鼓励物理教师在课堂上放映这部电影，以传达广义相对论的概念。”

7
00:00:52,400 --> 00:01:02,780
In fact, one of the executive producers of Interstellar was Kip Thorne, a professor of theoretical physics at the California Institute of Technology (Caltech).
事实上，《星际穿越》的执行制片人之一是加州理工学院（Caltech）的理论物理学教授基普·索恩（Kip Thorne）。

8
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:11,390
For him, films such as Interstellar, Contact and 2001: A Space Odyssey can inspire young people.
对他来说，像《星际穿越》、《接触》和《2001太空漫游》这样的电影可以激励年轻人。

9
00:01:11,390 --> 00:01:16,100
Blockbusters are improving when it comes to portraying scientific theories.
在描绘科学理论方面，大片正在不断进步。

10
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:27,840
An initiative by the US National Academy of Sciences has been putting proper scientists in touch with movie people to achieve a better result – which is vital in the internet age.
美国国家科学院的一项倡议一直以来让真正的科学家与电影人接触，以取得更好的效果——这在互联网时代至关重要。

11
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:35,030
Interstellar's director Christopher Nolan says: "Consumers have a lot more immediate access to information.
《星际穿越》的导演克里斯托弗·诺兰说：“消费者可以更直接地获取信息。

12
00:01:35,030 --> 00:01:47,750
If you go and see a film about a particular subject, particularly a true life story, you can go home and look it up on Wikipedia and see if the basic things portrayed in the film are true or not.
如果你去看一部关于特定主题的电影，尤其是一个真实的故事，你可以回家后在维基百科上查找，看看电影中描绘的基本内容是否真实。

13
00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:51,250
The same is true of science in the films".
电影中的科学也是如此。”

14
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:56,640
Professional scientists may no longer cringe in their seats when they watch sci-fi movies.
专业科学家在观看科幻电影时可能不再会在座位上感到尴尬。

15
00:01:56,640 --> 00:02:00,880
Today, getting the science wrong is no longer an option.
如今，已经不再允许科学内容继续出错。
